{"name":"Magenta Dye","hex":"#ca1f7b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"magenta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color which is close to the equal mixture of red and blue which is an additive secondary color but a subtractive primary color evoked by the combination of red and light blue."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the color of fuchsia, fuchsine, light purple."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magenta"},{"term":"dye","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorant, especially one that has an affinity to the substrate to which it is applied.","Any hue or color."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To colour with dye, or as if with dye."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dye"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dye","blocks":[{"text":"A dye is a colored substance that is soluble in some solvent; by contrast pigments are insoluble or nearly so in all solvents. Because of their solubility, dyes can chemically bind to the material they color. Dye is generally applied in an aqueous solution and may require a mordant to improve the fastness of the dye on the fiber."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/2019-11-22_Some_of_the_dyes_made_at_De_Kat.jpg/330px-2019-11-22_Some_of_the_dyes_made_at_De_Kat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dye","wikidata":"Q189720"},{"title":"Magenta","blocks":[{"text":"Magenta is a purplish-pink color. On color wheels of the RGB and CMYK color models, it is located directly midway between blue and red. It is one of the four colors of subtractive ink used in color printing by most color printers, also known as CMYK along with yellow, cyan, and black to make all the other colors and hues. The tone of magenta used in printing, printer's magenta, is redder than the magenta of the RGB (additive) model, the former being closer to rose."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Pink_swanboat_hosting_a_real_bird_on_its_head%2C_on_Shinobazu_Pond%2C_Ueno_Park%2C_Tokyo.jpg/330px-Pink_swanboat_hosting_a_real_bird_on_its_head%2C_on_Shinobazu_Pond%2C_Ueno_Park%2C_Tokyo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magenta","wikidata":"Q3276756"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Dyeing_British_Library_Royal_MS_15.E.iii%2C_f._269_1482.jpg/330px-Dyeing_British_Library_Royal_MS_15.E.iii%2C_f._269_1482.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Dyeing_British_Library_Royal_MS_15.E.iii%2C_f._269_1482.jpg/330px-Dyeing_British_Library_Royal_MS_15.E.iii%2C_f._269_1482.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dyeing wool cloth, 1482: from a French translation of Bartolomaeus Anglicus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADyeing_British_Library_Royal_MS_15.E.iii%2C_f._269_1482.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Childhood_Joy.jpg/500px-Childhood_Joy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Childhood_Joy.jpg/1280px-Childhood_Joy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Childhood_Joy.jpg/500px-Childhood_Joy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Drying colored cloth","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChildhood_Joy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Shelve_with_various_hair_colours_%28hair_dyes%29_in_a_hairdresser_shop_in_Germany_%282023%29.jpg/500px-Shelve_with_various_hair_colours_%28hair_dyes%29_in_a_hairdresser_shop_in_Germany_%282023%29.jpg?utm_s